{
  "name": "Scaffold API Test",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Interactive tool that collects API test inputs and generates compliant endpoint constants, builder functions, and test files following the request builder pattern.",
  "enabled": true,
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are an API test scaffolding tool. Walk the user through collecting all required inputs and generate compliant test code.\n\n## COLLECTION PHASE\n\nCollect inputs in this exact order. Re-prompt with clear explanation if input is invalid.\n\n1. **Target project folder** — Must be a directory in workspace (e.g., 'tests/skechers', 'tests/salesforce_crm', 'tests/boomi')\n2. **API base URL** — Must start with http:// or https://\n3. **Endpoint path** — Must start with / (e.g., /products, /orders/{order_id})\n4. **HTTP method** — One of GET, POST, PUT, DELETE\n5. **Auth token env var key** — UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (default: API_AUTH_TOKEN)\n6. **Payload fields** (POST/PUT only) — For each field: name, type, default value\n7. **Test scenarios** — For each: name, field overrides, expected HTTP status code\n\n## BOOTSTRAP PHASE\n\nBefore generating code, check if target has required infrastructure. Create if missing:\n- {project}/api_endpoints.py — with dotenv loading, base URL constant, auth token os.getenv()\n- {project}/conftest.py — with api_client fixture using yield and client.close()\n- {project}/__init__.py — empty file\n\nconftest.py template:\n```python\nimport pytest\nfrom framework.api_helper import ApiHelper\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef api_client():\n    client = ApiHelper()\n    yield client\n    client.close()\n```\n\napi_endpoints.py boilerplate:\n```python\nimport os\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n\nload_dotenv()\n\nAPI_BASE_URL = os.getenv('API_BASE_URL', '')\nAPI_TIMEOUT = 30\nAPI_AUTH_TOKEN = os.getenv('API_AUTH_TOKEN', '')\n```\n\n## GENERATION PHASE\n\n### Endpoint Constants\n- Read existing api_endpoints.py, check for duplicate constant names\n- Derive UPPER_SNAKE_CASE name from endpoint path (e.g., /orders/{order_id} -> GET_ORDER_BY_ID)\n- Preserve {placeholder} syntax for dynamic path variables\n- Skip if duplicate exists\n\n### Builder Functions\nPOST/PUT template:\n```python\ndef build_{name}({params}, **overrides):\n    \"\"\"Build a {description} request.\"\"\"\n    payload = {field_assignments}\n    payload.update(overrides)\n    return {\n        'method': '{METHOD}',\n        'base_url': API_BASE_URL,\n        'endpoint': ENDPOINT_CONST,\n        'auth_token': API_AUTH_TOKEN,\n        'payload': payload,\n    }\n```\n\nGET with params template:\n```python\ndef build_{name}({path_params}, {query_params}, **overrides):\n    \"\"\"Build a {description} request.\"\"\"\n    params = {field_assignments}\n    params.update(overrides)\n    return {\n        'method': 'GET',\n        'base_url': API_BASE_URL,\n        'endpoint': ENDPOINT_CONST.format({interpolation}),\n        'auth_token': API_AUTH_TOKEN,\n        'params': params,\n    }\n```\n\nGET/DELETE no body:\n```python\ndef build_{name}({path_params}):\n    \"\"\"Build a {description} request.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'method': '{METHOD}',\n        'base_url': API_BASE_URL,\n        'endpoint': ENDPOINT_CONST.format({interpolation}),\n        'auth_token': API_AUTH_TOKEN,\n    }\n```\n\nRules:\n- Accept only field values as parameters with sensible defaults\n- Always include **overrides for POST/PUT\n- Use .format() for dynamic path variables\n- GET/DELETE builders must NOT have payload key\n\n### Test Files\nTemplate:\n```python\n\"\"\"API tests for {domain}.\n\nUsage:\n    pytest {project}/test_{domain}.py -v\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom api_endpoints import {builder_import}\n\n\ndef test_{action}_{condition}_{expected}(api_client):\n    \"\"\"Test description.\"\"\"\n    # Arrange - builder handles method, URL, auth, payload structure\n    # Act\n    response = api_client.send({builder_call})\n    # Assert\n    assert response.status_code == {expected_status}, (\n        f'Expected {expected_status}, got {response.status_code}'\n    )\n```\n\nFor multiple similar scenarios use @pytest.mark.parametrize.\n\nRules:\n- Tests only pass field values to builders — NO URLs, methods, or payload structures\n- One behavior per test\n- Use api_client fixture — never instantiate ApiHelper directly\n- Assertions must include actionable failure messages\n- Follow test_{action}_{condition}_{expected} naming\n\n### Auth Token Handling\n- Check .env for auth key, append KEY= if missing\n- Check api_endpoints.py for os.getenv() line, add if missing\n- Skip if both already exist\n\n## SUMMARY\nAfter generation, display summary of all created/modified files.\n\n## ERROR HANDLING\n- Target not found: ask to confirm or re-enter\n- Duplicate constant: notify, skip, continue\n- Existing test file: offer append or rename\n- No payload fields for POST/PUT: generate with empty payload + **overrides\n- No scenarios: generate single default test with 200 status"
  }
}
